record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase3-rate-loop-cache-reuse-measured/1 : evidence {
    title "Rate-loop CandidateForwardCache cross-probe hit rate measured at ~96-97%; size cap not viable"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:844b5af100021b5fc048b15684a1d869181c4f7b
    command "cd JPXL &amp;&amp; cargo build --release -p jpxl-cli &amp;&amp; ./target/release/jpxl bench vardct-rate --input &lt;image&gt; --threads 1 --iters 1 --bpp 1.0 --diag"
    summary """
        Extended `jpxl bench vardct-rate --diag` to print a new rate_diag= line (fast_prices, full_prices, dct_cache_hits/misses/hit_rate from RateOutcome.stats, which already existed but was never surfaced -- previously only the last probe's per-plan_at diag= line printed, hiding cross-probe reuse entirely). Measured CandidateForwardCache's actual cross-probe hit rate on two images: 12MP (4000x3000) at bpp=1.0 ran 23 total probes (11 fast + 12 full) with 6,349,453 hits vs 245,575 misses = 96.28% hit rate; misses (245,575) closely match the ~245,228 unique candidates a single vardct-fixed probe computes, confirming every probe after the first is scoring the *same* candidate set (position+transform doesn't depend on quantizer scale, only block_cost's score of each does) and getting a near-total cache hit. 1024x768 at bpp=1.0 ran 25 probes (13+12), 497,050 hits vs 16,127 misses = 96.86% hit rate -- same pattern, size-independent. Conclusion: cross-probe reuse is real, large (~20-25x effective multiplier on forward-DCT work across a default-budget rate search), and a size-capped/evicting cache would have to retain essentially 100% of one frame's unique candidates to preserve it -- a cap cannot meaningfully shrink CandidateForwardCache's memory footprint without directly costing proportional wall-time (up to ~23x more forward-DCT recomputation for evicted-then-needed entries). This closes the "measure-then-cap" option from jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase3-forward-cache's note: it is not viable at this frame's candidate-set scale. The remaining path to outside-advice.md §7's ~428 MB reduction is §8's compact-per-candidate-summary redesign (score from summaries, materialize full coefficients only for the winner), which is a larger, separately-scoped change touching block_cost/tile_region's candidate representation, not an isolated cache-policy tweak.
        """
}

record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase3-selected-forward-clone-eliminated/1 : evidence {
    title "Phase-3 selected-forward clone eliminated, output byte-identical"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:78d8ffbc467cadc426c0381e25c613f11c847d62
    command "cd JPXL && cargo test -p jpxl-encode -p jpxl-encode-policy --lib --release && cargo test -p jpxl-encode-policy --test vardct_oracle --test vardct_roundtrip --test rate_loop && cargo build --release -p jpxl-cli && ./target/release/jpxl bench vardct-fixed --input &lt;12MP-P6&gt; --threads 1 --iters 1 --diag"
    summary """
        Split plan_at_with_cfl's per-group cover-selection loop into two passes: pass A does all cache-mutating work (cover selection + ensure_forwards_cached, a new helper that guarantees every selected varblock's forward is present, a no-op under CoverMode::Hierarchical which already inserted it during scoring, real work under CoverMode::FixedDct8x8 which never touches the cache) across every LF group; pass B (after all mutation is done) borrows &VarblockForward references via a new CandidateForwardCache::get() / gather_forward_refs(), replacing forward_selected's old fwd.clone(). estimate_cfl and quantize_group signatures updated from &[VarblockForward]/&[&[VarblockForward]] to &[&VarblockForward]/&[&[&VarblockForward]] (bodies unchanged, Rust auto-derefs through the extra reference). 12MP vardct-fixed threads=1 --diag: output_bytes and fingerprint IDENTICAL before/after (1,530,188 / 30e55ba3faef4d64), confirming this is purely representational -- sel_clones 41,949 -> 0, sel_bytes 144,000,000 -> 0. jpxl-encode + jpxl-encode-policy lib tests (59+103), vardct_roundtrip (12), rate_loop (11+1 ignored) all pass; vardct_oracle 9/10 passes, the one failure (both_oracles_decode_a_stream_from_the_hf_mul_segment) is the same pre-existing, unrelated failure documented against jpegxl-rs.work.arch-phase2-cfl-quant.
        """
}

